{"id":"17A","title":"Anger and Wrath","part":{"n":17,"title":"Personal character traits"},"url":"/law/17-personal-character-traits/17a","entries":[{"id":"17A.1","text":"Anger causes strife and transgression.","refs":[{"book":"Proverbs","chapter":15,"verses":"18"},{"book":"Proverbs","chapter":29,"verses":"8,22"},{"book":"Proverbs","chapter":30,"verses":"33"}],"citation":"Prov. 15:18; Prov. 29:8, 22; Prov. 30:33."},{"id":"17A.2","text":"Be not hasty in your spirit to be angry (be slow to anger).","refs":[{"book":"Ecclesiastes","chapter":7,"verses":"9"},{"book":"Proverbs","chapter":15,"verses":"18"},{"book":"Proverbs","chapter":16,"verses":"32"},{"book":"James","chapter":1,"verses":"19-20"}],"citation":"Eccl. 7:9; Prov. 15:18; Prov. 16:32; James 1:19-20."},{"id":"17A.3","text":"Anger without cause is condemned.","refs":[{"book":"Matthew","chapter":5,"verses":"22"}],"citation":"Matt. 5:22."},{"id":"17A.4","text":"Wrath is characteristic of fools.","refs":[{"book":"Proverbs","chapter":12,"verses":"16"},{"book":"Proverbs","chapter":14,"verses":"16,29"},{"book":"Proverbs","chapter":27,"verses":"3"},{"book":"Ecclesiastes","chapter":7,"verses":"9"}],"citation":"Prov. 12:16; Prov. 14:16, 29; Prov. 27:3; Eccl. 7:9."},{"id":"17A.5","text":"Be angry, and yet do not sin: do not let the sun go down on your wrath.","refs":[{"book":"Psalms","chapter":4,"verses":"4"},{"book":"Ephesians","chapter":4,"verses":"26"}],"citation":"Psa. 4:4; Eph. 4:26."},{"id":"17A.6","text":"Wrath is cruel.","refs":[{"book":"Genesis","chapter":49,"verses":"7"},{"book":"Proverbs","chapter":27,"verses":"4"}],"citation":"Gen. 49:7; Prov. 27:4."},{"id":"17A.7","text":"Cease from anger, and forsake wrath, let them be put away from you.","refs":[{"book":"Psalms","chapter":37,"verses":"8"},{"book":"Ephesians","chapter":4,"verses":"31"},{"book":"Colossians","chapter":3,"verses":"8"}],"citation":"Psa. 37:8; Eph. 4:31; Col. 3:8."},{"id":"17A.8","text":"A man's discretion makes him slow to anger, and it is to his glory to overlook transgression.","refs":[{"book":"Proverbs","chapter":19,"verses":"11"}],"citation":"Prov. 19:11."},{"id":"17A.9","text":"Anger and wrath brings its own punishment.","refs":[{"book":"Job","chapter":5,"verses":"2"},{"book":"Proverbs","chapter":19,"verses":"19"},{"book":"Proverbs","chapter":25,"verses":"28"}],"citation":"Job 5:2; Prov. 19:19; Prov. 25:28."},{"id":"17A.10","text":"A gentle answer turns away wrath, but a harsh word stirs up anger.","refs":[{"book":"Proverbs","chapter":15,"verses":"1"}],"citation":"Prov. 15:1."},{"id":"17A.11","text":"Children are not to be provoked to anger.","refs":[{"book":"Ephesians","chapter":6,"verses":"4"},{"book":"Colossians","chapter":3,"verses":"21"}],"citation":"Eph. 6:4; Col. 3:21."},{"id":"17A.12","text":"He who is quick-tempered acts foolishly, but he who is slow to wrath has great understanding.","refs":[{"book":"Proverbs","chapter":14,"verses":"17,29"}],"citation":"Prov. 14:17, 29."},{"id":"17A.13","text":"Anger can be justifiable, as exemplified by: Christ - Mark 3:5. Jacob - Gen. 31:36. Moses - Exod.11:18; 32:19; Lev. 10:16. Nehemiah -","refs":[{"book":"Nehemiah","chapter":5,"verses":"6"}],"citation":"Neh. 5:6; 13:17,25."},{"id":"17A.14","text":"Let every man be swift to hear, slow to speak, slow to wrath; for the wrath of man does not produce the righteousness of God.","refs":[{"book":"James","chapter":1,"verses":"19-20"}],"citation":"James 1: 19-20."}]}